{
  "id": "https://m-lancini.github.io/frida-vocab/dictionary/situations-of-risk",
  "type": "Concept",
  "prefLabel": {
    "en": "situations of risk"
  },
  "definition": {
    "en": "Contexts in which a person's life, safety, integrity or effective exercise of rights may be seriously threatened."
  },
  "scopeNote": {
    "en": [
      "The expression shifts the focus away from a supposed intrinsic vulnerability of the person towards the external conditions that increase exposure to harm — armed conflict, humanitarian emergencies, natural disasters, displacement, institutionalisation or barriers to accessing information and services: it is a category centred on the context, not on a fixed identity. Art. 11 CRPD requires States to ensure the protection and safety of persons with disabilities in such situations, and the OHCHR study on that provision interprets it from a human rights approach, moving beyond welfare-based or medical readings. The response must be inclusive and accessible at every stage – prevention, evacuation, rescue, care and recovery –, with understandable information, the provision of supports and the participation of the persons affected themselves, including women and children with disabilities."
    ]
  },
  "notation": [
    "10.9"
  ],
  "broader": {
    "id": "https://m-lancini.github.io/frida-vocab/dictionary/section-10",
    "prefLabel": {
      "en": "Rights, legal capacity and access to justice"
    }
  },
